# WatchSeeBuy

This repo is **WatchSeeBuy** (`watchseebuy.com`). Watch. See. Buy.

Become the CamelCamelCamel of eBay for everyday buyers — not a faster eBay, not a flipper-alert tool.

## Locked decisions

- **Name:** WatchSeeBuy. Never use eBay, Bay, or eBuy in the brand or domain.
- **First vertical:** collectibles (cards, Lego, vintage toys, comics, coins, stamps, memorabilia).
- **Core loop:** search acquires; **watches** are the product and the EPN engine.
- **Auth gate:** search and sold comps are public. Account required only to save a watch or receive alerts. SSO: Google, Facebook, Apple. Email magic link as fallback. Optional ship-to on the search page; do not block search behind signup.
- **Watches are intent**, not a clone of eBay saved-search params. Natural-language criteria, then explain why a listing matches.
- **Landed cost is the number** people set (item + shipping + simple import/tax to their address). Location is first-class.
- **Sold-comp context** on every result and every alert (condition-matched).
- **Quiet alerts** over volume. Compete on accuracy, not 15-second poll speed.
- **Official eBay APIs only.** EPN software-application approval required before sending users to eBay. Design for a short affiliate cookie (one-tap from the alert).
- **Ad blockers:** probe the real EPN host. If blocked, dismissible banner + fallback to a plain eBay item URL. Never cloak affiliate links or break Buy.
- **Quota increase on first live deploy.** File eBay Application Growth Check as soon as production is up. Instrument calls/day, cache hits, and 429s from day one so the request has a formula, not a guess. EPN approval and API quota are separate gates.
- **Web first.** Mobile later, as a notification surface.
- **Consumer core stays free.** EPN is default revenue. Do not hide basic watches behind a $20–40/mo wall.

## Do not build

Sniping, multi-marketplace reseller dashboards, scrapers, Telegram speed races, or a generic “all of eBay but simpler” homepage.

## Stack (locked)

Modular monolith on GCP. TypeScript, Next.js web, TypeScript worker, Cloud SQL Postgres. Official eBay APIs only. Coalesce watches into shared coverage queries — never poll once per user.

Not now: GKE, a microservice per noun, scrapers, Firestore as system of record.

Read `PRODUCT.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` before adding features.
